  "title": "First Night of Friday (Laylat al-Raghaib)",
  "data": "Prayer of Laylat al-Raghaib\nObserve fasting on the first Thursday in Rajab.\nBetween the Maghrib (sunset) and Isha’ (evening) Prayers, offer a twelve unit prayer, ending each set of two units with Taslim (i.e. the concluding part of a ritual prayer).\nIn each unit, recite [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once, [Surah al-Qadr](A101) three times, and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) twelve times.\nAfter the prayer, repeat 70 times:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ النَّبِيِّ الْاُمِّيِّ وَعَلٰى اٰلِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADENIN NABIYYIL UMMIYYE WA A’LAA AALEHI.\nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, the Unlettered Prophet, and upon his family.\nThen prostrate and repeat this litany 70 times:\nسُبُّوْحٌ قُدُّوْسٌ رَبُّ الْمَلَاۤئِكَةِ وَالرُّوْحِ\nSUBBOOHUN QUDDOOSUN RABBUL MALAA-EKATE WAR ROOHE.\nPerfectly Pure, Infinitely Holy, Lord of the Angels and the Spirit.\nThen raise your head from prostration and repeat 70 times:\nرَبِّ اغْفِرْ وَارْحَمْ وَتَجَاوَزْ عَمَّا تَعْلَمُ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَلِيُّ الْاَعْظَمُ\nRABBIGH FIR WAR HAM WA TAJAAWAZ A’MMAA TA’LAMO INNAKA ANTAL A’LIYYUL A-A’ZAM.\nMy Lord, forgive and have mercy, and overlook [the sins] that You know. Indeed, You are the Most High, the Greatest.\nThen prostrate again and repeat the same litany 70 times:\nسُبُّوْحٌ قُدُّوْسٌ رَبُّ الْمَلَاۤئِكَةِ وَالرُّوْحِ\nSUBBOOHUN QUDDOOSUN RABBUL MALAA-EKATE WAR ROOHE.\nPerfectly Pure, Infinitely Holy, Lord of the Angels and the Spirit.\nThen ask Almighty Allah for your needs; they will surely be granted, God willing.",
  "tabs": [
    "Visit, Umrah & Dua in Prostration\nVisit the Holy Shrine of Imam al-Reza (a.s.) in Rajab.\nGo on Umrah in Rajab.\nWhile prostrating, recite:\nعَظُمَ الذَّنْبُ مِنْ عَبْدِكَ فَلْيَحْسُنِ الْعَفْوُ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ\nA’ZOMAZ ZANBO MIN A’BDEKA FALYAHSONIL A’FWO MIN I’NDEKA\nThe sin from Your servant has become great, so let the forgiveness from You be beautiful."
